-- title:
--   Pro-étale cohomology of $\varprojlim \nu^*F_n$ is the limit of the levelwise cohomology under a Mittag-Leffler condition
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a scheme and let $(F_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be an inverse system of sheaves of abelian groups on the small étale site of $S$ whose transition maps $F_{n+1} \to F_n$ are epimorphisms. Let $\nu^*$ denote pullback of sheaves from the étale to the pro-étale site of $S$, and let $\mathbb{Z}$ be the constant pro-étale sheaf, so that $\operatorname{Ext}^j(\mathbb{Z}, -) = H^j(S_{\text{proét}}, -)$. Fix $i \in \mathbb{N}$ and assume that the inverse system of abelian groups
--   $$n \longmapsto \operatorname{Ext}^i(\mathbb{Z}, \nu^* F_n)$$
--   satisfies the Mittag-Leffler condition. Then the canonical map induced by the limit projections
--   $$\operatorname{Ext}^{i+1}\big(\mathbb{Z}, \varprojlim_n \nu^* F_n\big) \longrightarrow \varprojlim_n \operatorname{Ext}^{i+1}(\mathbb{Z}, \nu^* F_n)$$
--   is bijective (the limit on the left is taken in pro-étale sheaves).
--
--   This is the $\varprojlim^1$-free case of Jannsen's exact sequence relating continuous cohomology to the cohomology of the limit sheaf, in the form of a statement about the canonical comparison map; it feeds the comparison of $\ell$-adic cohomology with pro-étale cohomology.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Universe: $S$ is in `Scheme.{u}` and sheaves take values in `Ab.{u+1}`. The constant sheaf is `proetaleConstantUnit S` (with values `ULift ℤ`), the pullback is `ProEt.sheafPullback S Ab.{u+1}`, the comparison map is `Ext.extLimitToLimit`, and the levelwise Ext groups are `extFunctorObj (proetaleConstantUnit S) i`. The Mittag-Leffler condition is Mathlib's `Functor.IsMittagLeffler` applied to the underlying system of sets (composed with `forget`). Epimorphic transitions are `Epi (SequentialSystem.transition F n)`. Note the shift: the hypothesis is in degree $i$, the conclusion in degree $i+1$. The theorem is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.bijective_extLimitToLimit_of_isMittagLeffler`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Topology/Comparison/LimitComparison.lean, lines 241-464 (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.bijective_extLimitToLimit_of_isMittagLeffler`).

